aised Democrat Katy Padilla Stout substantially, but he has drawn heavy outside opposition spending and sustained negative coverage over crude and offensive remarks, with even his own party's leadership defending him reluctantly.\n\nExpert raters mostly place the race at Likely or Lean Republican, with one outlet calling it a Tossup. Prediction markets price Democratic chances around 40 percent. The only available poll, from March and Democratic-sponsored, showed a two-point race. The forecast lands at a modest Republican edge with wide uncertainty, reflecting the district's lean against a flawed nominee and thin polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}]}